%% Loom Workflow Diagrams
%% Location: analysis/workflows.mermaid
%% Documentation: See 04-business-logic.md for detailed algorithm documentation

%% Diagram 1: Agent Conversation Flow
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> WaitingForUserInput: Agent created

    WaitingForUserInput --> CallingLlm: User sends message
    CallingLlm --> CallingLlm: LLM streaming text
    CallingLlm --> ProcessingLlmResponse: LLM completes

    ProcessingLlmResponse --> ExecutingTools: LLM requests tools
    ProcessingLlmResponse --> WaitingForUserInput: LLM responds normally

    ExecutingTools --> ExecutingTools: Tools running
    ExecutingTools --> PostToolsHook: All tools complete (mutating)
    ExecutingTools --> CallingLlm: All tools complete (read-only)

    PostToolsHook --> CallingLlm: Hook complete

    CallingLlm --> Error: LLM error
    Error --> CallingLlm: Retry timeout
    Error --> WaitingForUserInput: Max retries

    WaitingForUserInput --> [*]: Shutdown
    CallingLlm --> [*]: Shutdown
    ExecutingTools --> [*]: Shutdown
    Error --> [*]: Shutdown

%% Diagram 2: Tool Execution Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant Agent
    participant ToolRegistry
    participant Tool
    participant Filesystem

    Agent->>ToolRegistry: invoke(tool_name, args)
    ToolRegistry->>Tool: invoke(args, context)

    Tool->>Tool: Validate path in workspace
    alt Path valid
        Tool->>Filesystem: Read/Edit file
        Filesystem-->>Tool: Result
        Tool-->>ToolRegistry: Ok(output)
    else Path invalid
        Tool-->>ToolRegistry: Err(PathOutsideWorkspace)
    end

    ToolRegistry-->>Agent: Result

    Agent->>Agent: Add tool result to conversation
    Agent->>Agent: Check if all tools complete
    Agent->>Agent: Determine next action

%% Diagram 3: Authentication Flow (OAuth)
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant CLI
    participant Server
    participant OAuthProvider

    User->>CLI: loom login
    CLI->>Server: GET /auth/github/start
    Server->>Server: Generate state token
    Server->>Server: Store in session
    Server-->>CLI: 302 Redirect to GitHub
    CLI->>User: Open browser

    User->>OAuthProvider: Visit auth URL
    OAuthProvider->>User: Display approval page
    User->>OAuthProvider: Authorize
    OAuthProvider-->>Server: Callback with code
    Server->>OAuthProvider: Exchange code for token
    OAuthProvider-->>Server: Access token
    Server->>Server: Fetch user profile
    Server->>Server: Create/update user
    Server->>Server: Create session
    Server-->>User: Redirect to success page
    Server-->>CLI: Session token
    CLI->>CLI: Store credentials

%% Diagram 4: Thread Persistence Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant Agent
    participant ThreadStore
    participant Database

    Agent->>ThreadStore: upsert(thread)
    ThreadStore->>Database: SELECT thread BY id

    alt Thread not found
        ThreadStore->>Database: INSERT thread (version=1)
    else Thread exists
        ThreadStore->>ThreadStore: Check version
        alt Version mismatch
            ThreadStore-->>Agent: Err(VersionConflict)
        else Version matches
            ThreadStore->>ThreadStore: Increment version
            ThreadStore->>Database: UPDATE thread
            ThreadStore->>Database: UPDATE git_commits
            ThreadStore->>Database: UPDATE threads_fts
        end
    end

    ThreadStore-->>Agent: Ok(thread)

%% Diagram 5: Auto-Commit Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant Agent
    participant AutoCommitService
    participant Git

    Agent->>AutoCommitService: RunPostToolsHook(completed_tools)
    AutoCommitService->>AutoCommitService: Check for mutating tools

    alt Mutating tools succeeded
        AutoCommitService->>Git: git status --porcelain
        Git-->>AutoCommitService: Changed files

        alt Changes detected
            AutoCommitService->>AutoCommitService: Generate commit message
            AutoCommitService->>Git: git add <files>
            AutoCommitService->>Git: git commit -m "message"
            Git-->>AutoCommitService: Commit SHA
            AutoCommitService-->>Agent: Success(sha)
        else No changes
            AutoCommitService-->>Agent: Skipped
        end
    else No mutating tools
        AutoCommitService-->>Agent: Skipped
    end

    Agent->>Agent: Continue conversation

%% Diagram 6: LLM Request Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI
    participant ProxyLlmClient
    participant Server
    participant AnthropicAPI

    CLI->>ProxyLlmClient: complete_streaming(request)
    ProxyLlmClient->>Server: POST /llm/stream
    Note over Server: Route to provider

    Server->>AnthropicAPI: POST /v1/messages
    Server->>Server: Stream SSE events

    loop For each chunk
        AnthropicAPI-->>Server: data chunk
        Server-->>ProxyLlmClient: SSE event
        ProxyLlmClient->>ProxyLlmClient: Parse delta
        ProxyLlmClient-->>CLI: LlmEvent::TextDelta
        CLI->>CLI: Display to user
    end

    AnthropicAPI-->>Server: message_stop
    Server-->>ProxyLlmClient: LlmEvent::Completed
    ProxyLlmClient-->>CLI: LlmResponse

%% Diagram 7: Device Code Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI
    participant Server
    participant User
    participant OAuthProvider

    CLI->>Server: POST /auth/device/start
    Server->>Server: Generate codes
    Server-->>CLI: device_code, user_code, verification_url

    CLI->>User: "Enter code XYZ at https://example.com"

    User->>OAuthProvider: Visit verification URL
    User->>OAuthProvider: Enter user code
    OAuthProvider->>User: Show authorization
    User->>OAuthProvider: Approve
    OAuthProvider-->>Server: Webhook: code approved

    loop Device polling
        CLI->>Server: POST /auth/device/poll (device_code)
        alt Not approved yet
            Server-->>CLI: status: pending
        else Approved
            Server-->>CLI: status: completed, access_token
        end
    end

    CLI->>CLI: Store credentials

%% Diagram 8: Feature Flag Evaluation Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant SDK
    participant Server
    participant Database

    SDK->>Server: POST /flags/evaluate
    Server->>Server: Parse request (person_id, flag_name)

    Server->>Database: SELECT flag BY name
    Database-->>Server: FeatureFlag (enabled, conditions)

    Server->>Server: Evaluate conditions:
    Note over Server: - Rollout percentage<br/>- Person whitelist<br/>- Attribute targeting

    Server->>Database: SELECT person BY id
    Database-->>Server: Person (attributes)

    Server->>Server: Check matches:
    Note over Server: - Is person in whitelist?<br/>- Within rollout %?<br/>- Attributes match?

    Server-->>SDK: { enabled: bool, reason: string }
    SDK->>SDK: Enable/disable feature

%% Diagram 9: Weaver Provisioning Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI
    participant Server
    participant Kubernetes
    participant Registry

    CLI->>Server: POST /weavers (image, env, resources)
    Server->>Server: Validate request
    Server->>Server: Generate weaver ID
    Server->>Database: Insert weaver record

    Server->>Kubernetes: Create Pod
    Note over Kubernetes: - Pull container image<br/>- Inject secrets<br/>- Set resource limits

    Kubernetes-->>Server: Pod created
    Server-->>CLI: WeaverApiResponse (id, status: Pending)

    Kubernetes->>Registry: Pull image
    Kubernetes->>Kubernetes: Start container
    Kubernetes-->>Server: Status: Running

    Server->>CLI: WebSocket update (status: Running)

    CLI->>CLI: Attach to weaver
    Note over CLI: Execute commands remotely

    Kubernetes->>Kubernetes: Container exits
    Kubernetes-->>Server: Status: Succeeded
    Server->>Database: Update weaver status

%% Diagram 10: Analytics Event Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant SDK
    participant Server
    participant Queue
    participant Worker
    participant Database

    SDK->>Server: POST /analytics/events
    Server->>Server: Validate events
    Server->>Server: Resolve person ID:
    Note over Server: - Check existing person<br/>- Create new if needed

    Server->>Queue: Enqueue events
    Server-->>SDK: 202 Accepted

    Queue->>Worker: Dequeue batch
    Worker->>Database: Insert events (bulk)
    Worker->>Database: Update person properties
    Worker->>Database: Trigger aggregations

    Note over Database: - Funnel calculations<br/>- Retention analysis<br/>- Cohort reports

%% Diagram 11: Search Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLI
    participant Server
    participant FTS5
    participant Database

    CLI->>Server: GET /threads/search?q=query
    Server->>FTS5: SELECT FROM threads_fts WHERE threads_fts MATCH query
    Note over FTS5: BM25 ranking algorithm

    FTS5-->>Server: Thread IDs with scores
    Server->>Database: SELECT threads WHERE id IN (...)
    Database-->>Server: Thread data

    Server->>Server: Filter by visibility
    Server->>Server: Apply pagination
    Server-->>CLI: SearchResponse (hits with scores)

%% Diagram 12: Secret Injection Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant Server
    participant SecretStore
    participant Kubernetes
    participant Weaver

    Server->>SecretStore: GET secrets (repo_id, org_id)
    SecretStore->>SecretStore: Decrypt secrets
    SecretStore-->>Server: Secret map

    Server->>Kubernetes: Create Pod with secrets
    Note over Kubernetes: Inject as env vars<br/>or volume mounts

    Kubernetes->>Weaver: Start container
    Note over Weaver: Secrets available as<br/>environment variables

    Weaver->>Weaver: Access secrets via env
    Note over Weaver: - LOOM_SECRET_KEY=***<br/>- GIT_TOKEN=***

